<title>USA: KOCH OIL CUTS U.S. POSTED CRUDE PRICES 50 CTS/BBL.</title>
<headline>KOCH OIL CUTS U.S. POSTED CRUDE PRICES 50 CTS/BBL.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 50 cents a barrel, effective Wednesday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.25 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $15.50 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $17.75 and Oklahoma sweet is $18.25.</p>
<p>((--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620))</p>
